  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 142 AM CDT Fri Sep 25 2026\n\nRidging continues to build over the region today into a pseudo Rex \nblock with a nor'easter off the coast through the weekend. Cloud \ncover has finally given way to clearer skies and slightly warmer \ntemps. Expecting some increasing mid level clouds today and highs in \nthe mid-upper 70s through the weekend along with dry conditions.\n\nSoutherly flow returns early next week along with a slight warming \ntrend back into the 80s as the block breaks down and ridging reforms \nover the region. Mid to late next week still has the potential to be \nwet with an approaching southern stream low pressure system. There \nis better model agreement than last night but there are still some \nkey differences primarily in timing and placement. NBM still has \nPoPs increasing from west to east Tuesday night and continuing area \nwide through Friday (30-60%). This whole period will not be \ncontinuously wet, there will be dry periods. This PoP distribution \nis due to the timing differences in the models most likely. \nTemperatures look to remain in the 80s through next week.",
